# Maintenance mode kill switch.
# When set to "true", middleware rewrites every non-allowlisted request to
# the /maintenance page with a 503 status (and JSON 503 for /api/* callers,
# so the iOS shell doesn't try to parse HTML). The AASA file, _next assets,
# and the favicon stay reachable so iOS Universal Links keep working and the
# maintenance page itself can render. Flip to "true" only during host
# cutovers or planned downtime.
MAINTENANCE_MODE=false

# Number of reverse proxies in front of the app, used to extract the real
# client IP from X-Forwarded-For for rate limiting (login brute-force cap,
# OAuth signup cap). Default 1 = a single trusted edge proxy (Coolify/Traefik),
# making the rightmost XFF entry the client. Set to 2 if you put a CDN (e.g.
# Cloudflare) in front of Traefik — otherwise every visitor keys on the CDN's
# shared egress IP and shares one rate-limit bucket.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# ─── Upstash Redis — rate limiting (REQUIRED in production) ─────────────────
# Backs every rate limiter (login/signup caps and the cost-limited AI routes).
# REQUIRED in production: the cost limiter fails CLOSED, so if these are unset
# the AI routes reject every request. In development the cost limiter fails
# OPEN, so local work without Redis still functions. Find them in the Upstash
# console → your Redis database → "REST API".
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare Turnstile — bot gate on signup + password-reset. BOTH keys are
# REQUIRED in production; missing or partial configuration fails closed.
# Development and tests may leave both blank for no-op behavior. Create a
# widget at Cloudflare dashboard → Turnstile
# (add notemage.app and localhost as hostnames). The site key is public; the
# secret key is server-only. NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined at BUILD time, so
# set NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY in Coolify's BUILD env, not just runtime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Pre-launch signup bypass token. While signups are paused (the middleware
# redirects /auth/register → /waitlist), visiting
# /auth/register?key=<this-token> drops an HttpOnly `signup_bypass` cookie
# and unlocks the register page, the credentials API, and OAuth account
# creation for that browser only. Leave unset to keep signups paused for
# everyone. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# SIGNUP_BYPASS_TOKEN=

# Database connection string
# Format: postgresql://USERNAME:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?schema=SCHEMA
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://notemage:dev_password@db:5432/notemage_dev?schema=public"

# ─── Supabase Storage (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by signed-URL uploads (Mage chat attachments, page/flashcard images,
# imports, avatars). Read server-side in src/lib/supabase.ts — both must be
# set in the container runtime env or every upload route returns 500.
# Find them in Supabase → Project Settings → API.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL  → "Project URL"  (https://xxxxx.supabase.co)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY → "service_role" secret (NOT the anon key)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Authentication (Phase 3). NEXTAUTH_SECRET is also the HMAC key for opaque
# per-email login-throttle keys. Rotate it with the auth-security release to
# invalidate every pre-authVersion session.
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-secret
# NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Claude API (Phase 7)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# ─── Google Gemini — PDF import structure engine ───────────────────────────
# The PDF-import pipeline's vision pass (src/lib/pdf-import/engine-gemini.ts)
# sends each rendered page to Gemini to classify its structure. A server-only
# runtime secret — set it in the Coolify container env, NOT with a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# When unset, import still works: every page falls back to the deterministic
# heuristic extractor (lower fidelity, but never hard-fails).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
#
# Optional override for the Gemini model id — Google rotates ids. Defaults to
# gemini-2.5-flash-lite when unset.
# GEMINI_PDF_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# ─── Learning-path generation provider routing ─────────────────────────────
# Path generation (Stage A structure + Stage B theory/flashcards/quiz)
# defaults to Anthropic Claude (Haiku for everything except `plan.ultra`
# quizzes, which upgrade to Sonnet). To route some or all stages through
# Gemini 2.5 Flash instead, set the env vars below. GEMINI_API_KEY above is
# reused — no new key needed.
#
# `PATH_PROVIDER` sets the default for every stage; per-stage overrides win.
# Allowed values: 'anthropic' | 'gemini'. Unknown values are ignored.
# `plan.ultra=true` always forces Anthropic+Sonnet on the quiz stage
# regardless of these settings (the existing ultra-path UX is preserved).
# PATH_PROVIDER=anthropic
# PATH_PROVIDER_STRUCTURE=
# PATH_PROVIDER_THEORY=
# PATH_PROVIDER_FLASHCARDS=
# PATH_PROVIDER_QUIZ=
#
# Optional override for the Gemini model id used by path generation —
# defaults to gemini-2.5-flash. Don't use the Lite variant here: the
# 11-question-kind quiz schema is more reliable on Flash.
# GEMINI_PATH_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# AI path generation — POST /api/learn/paths, the chat "make me a plan" flow,
# and exam study-plan generation all share the `ai_study_plan` meter — is a
# Pro feature and is BLOCKED for FREE users. There is no FREE allowance; FREE
# users upgrade to Pro to generate paths.

# Native video ingestion — Lane 2 (video-context plan §P2/§P3). All optional;
# code falls back to the defaults shown if unset.
# `VIDEO_INGEST_MODEL`: Gemini token for the native video call — flash | flash-lite
#   (Gemini-forced; an Anthropic token is ignored). Default: flash.
# `VIDEO_IMPORT_DISABLED`: master kill switch for Lane 2 (1/true = feature off).
#   Off-in-prod-until-tested. Default: off.
# `VIDEO_INGEST_MAX_DURATION_SEC`: hard per-video duration cap; pre-flight rejects
#   longer videos before any meter charge. Default: 3600 (60 min at low res).
# `VIDEO_INGEST_COST_CEILING_USD`: per-job input-cost ceiling; pre-flight aborts
#   before the model call if the estimate exceeds it. Default: 0.5.
# `VIDEO_INGEST_MEDIA_RESOLUTION`: token-rate control — low (~100 tok/s) | default
#   (~300 tok/s). Default: low.
# VIDEO_INGEST_MODEL=flash
# VIDEO_IMPORT_DISABLED=1
# VIDEO_INGEST_MAX_DURATION_SEC=3600
# VIDEO_INGEST_COST_CEILING_USD=0.5
# VIDEO_INGEST_MEDIA_RESOLUTION=low

# `WEB_SEARCH_DISABLED`: kill switch for Mage's OpenRouter web-search plugin
# (1 = disable web fetching; grants/quota still function, they just never search).
# WEB_SEARCH_DISABLED=1

# Weakness Training — Phase 1A passive concept-level diagnosis (plans/weakness-training.md).
# `WEAKNESS_TRAINING_CONCEPTS`: master flag for the concept layer (1 = on). When off
#   (default) path-gen tool schemas are byte-identical to pre-feature, the attempts
#   route adds only a short-circuited `if`, and no concept tables are written — i.e.
#   zero behaviour change. When on: closed-enum concept tags are emitted at path
#   generation, graded answers passively update ConceptMastery (post-commit, best-effort),
#   and untagged slots enqueue a cheap classify backfill. Keep OFF until 1A QA (≥10 paths,
#   tags finer than slot titles for ≥70% of slots) + the grading-route latency check pass.
# `CONCEPT_BACKFILL_MODEL`: optional model override for the slot-backfill classifier
#   (cheap tier; mirrors EXAM_WEAK_ANALYSIS_MODEL). Default: unset (cheap tier).
# WEAKNESS_TRAINING_CONCEPTS=1
# CONCEPT_BACKFILL_MODEL=haiku
#
# Weakness Training — Phase 1B user-facing remediation surfaces.
# `WEAKNESS_TRAINING_UI`: gate for the `/profile/weak-spots` page and
#   `POST /api/weakness/sessions` (1 = on). Independent of
#   WEAKNESS_TRAINING_CONCEPTS above. Default: off.
# `WEAKNESS_SESSION_MODEL`: optional model override for the remediation-session
#   generator (mirrors EXAM_MOCK_QUESTIONS_MODEL / path-quiz routing tier).
#   Default: unset (glm-sonnet tier).
# WEAKNESS_TRAINING_UI=1
# WEAKNESS_SESSION_MODEL=sonnet

# Microsoft OneNote Import (Phase 6 — Azure App Registration)
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=your-azure-client-id
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-azure-client-secret
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=common
#
# Encryption key for the Microsoft OAuth tokens in microsoft_connections — the
# access + refresh tokens are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest, never plaintext.
# A 32-byte key, base64- or hex-encoded. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Server-only secret (NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix). It is SEPARATE from
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET — do not reuse that value. Set it in your local .env.local AND
# in the Coolify prod container env. When unset, connect/import fail loudly
# instead of storing tokens in the clear.
# MS_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# YouTube Data API v3 (Scholar video recommendations)
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-youtube-api-key

# Resend (waitlist & transactional emails)
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev

# Sentry Error Monitoring (Phase 10)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@sentry.io/xxx
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=your-sentry-auth-token
# SENTRY_ORG=your-sentry-org
# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-sentry-project

# ─── PostHog Product Analytics (EU region) ─────────────────────────────────
# Project API key — a public "phc_..." value that ships in the browser bundle
# by design, so the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is correct. Find it in
# PostHog → Settings → Project → "Project API key". The same key is used by
# the browser SDK (src/components/analytics/PostHogProvider.tsx) and the
# server SDK (src/lib/analytics/posthog-server.ts). Leave it unset to disable
# analytics entirely — both SDKs no-op when the key is missing.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined at BUILD time: set this in Coolify's build
# environment, not just the runtime env, or the browser SDK won't see it.
#
# Capture is consent-gated (opt-out by default) — nothing is sent and no
# cookies are set until optInAnalytics() runs (src/lib/analytics/consent.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── OAuth: Continue with Google ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized redirect URI: {NEXTAUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google
# Scopes requested by next-auth's GoogleProvider: openid, email, profile.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#
# Native (iOS shell) Google sign-in goes through /api/auth/native/google
# instead of the redirect handshake (Google blocks OAuth in embedded WebViews).
# Create a SEPARATE OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "iOS" (bundle id
# app.notemage.mobile) and set the id token's audience allowlist below. The same
# value must be set as EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID (or app.json
# extra.googleIosClientId) in apps/mobile, and its REVERSED form added to
# ios/Notemage/Info.plist CFBundleURLTypes (com.googleusercontent.apps.<id>).
# GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# Optional: comma-separated allowlist if you add more native clients later.
# GOOGLE_NATIVE_CLIENT_IDS=...apps.googleusercontent.com,...apps.googleusercontent.com

# ─── OAuth: Continue with Apple (Sign in with Apple) ───────────────────────
# Requires an Apple Developer account + a Services ID + a .p8 key file.
# Steps (one-time setup):
#   1. developer.apple.com → Identifiers → create a Services ID. This value
#      is APPLE_ID (e.g. app.notemage.auth).
#   2. Enable "Sign In with Apple" on the Services ID and add the return URL:
#      {NEXTAUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/apple
#   3. Keys → create a new key with "Sign in with Apple" enabled. Download the
#      .p8 file — the Key ID is APPLE_KEY_ID, your 10-char team ID from the
#      account page is APPLE_TEAM_ID.
#   4. Generate a client_secret JWT (valid up to 6 months) — this is the
#      APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET env var below. Rotate before expiry.
#      Quick script (bash, requires `jwt` cli or a tiny node snippet using
#      jsonwebtoken):
#        const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
#        const fs = require('fs');
#        const key = fs.readFileSync('./AuthKey_XXXXXX.p8');
#        const token = jwt.sign({}, key, {
#          algorithm: 'ES256',
#          expiresIn: '180d',
#          audience: 'https://appleid.apple.com',
#          issuer: 'YOUR_TEAM_ID',
#          subject: 'app.notemage.auth',  // your Services ID
#          keyid: 'YOUR_KEY_ID',
#        });
#        console.log(token);
#      Paste the result as APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET below.
# APPLE_ID=app.notemage.auth
# APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET=eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6Ii4uLiJ9...

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two channels, one account: Lemon Squeezy (web + desktop, Merchant of Record —
# replaces Paddle, which declined our application) and RevenueCat (iOS App Store
# IAP). Both webhooks converge on User.tier — the app gates features on tier
# regardless of how the user paid.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* are inlined at BUILD time — set them in Coolify's BUILD env.
# The unprefixed secrets are read at RUNTIME — set them in Coolify's runtime env.

# Lemon Squeezy — browser (build-time). The generic product URL shows LS's own
# cadence picker; used as the fallback when no per-interval URL is set below.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<product-uuid>
# Optional per-cadence variant buy URLs — set these so the weekly/monthly/yearly
# toggle (signup + pricing) opens that variant pre-selected instead of the picker.
# Each is the variant's own "Share" buy URL from the LS dashboard. If a value is
# unset the toggle gracefully falls back to the generic product URL above.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_WEEKLY=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<weekly-variant-uuid>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_MONTHLY=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<monthly-variant-uuid>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_YEARLY=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<yearly-variant-uuid>
# PPP price-group variants (CHF 1.30/4.20/34 — see PPP_PRICE in tiers.ts).
# Visitors whose IP-resolved currency is INR/BRL/TRY check out on these; unset
# values gracefully fall back to the base-price URLs above.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_WEEKLY_PPP=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<weekly-ppp-variant-uuid>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_MONTHLY_PPP=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<monthly-ppp-variant-uuid>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL_YEARLY_PPP=https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/<yearly-ppp-variant-uuid>

# Lemon Squeezy — server (runtime)
# LEMONSQUEEZY_API_KEY=                                     # /sync, cancel, portal URL
# LEMONSQUEEZY_PRO_VARIANT_IDS=                             # comma list of ALL Pro variant ids (wk,mo,yr + the 3 PPP variants) — all map to PRO
# LEMONSQUEEZY_PRO_WEEKLY_VARIANT_IDS=                      # comma list of the weekly variant ids (base + PPP) — weekly quota resets weekly (tiers.ts); unset → all Pro subs are monthly-quota
# LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=                              # verifies X-Signature on the webhook

# RevenueCat (iOS — Phase B)
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH=                                  # static Authorization header the RC webhook must send
# REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY=                               # optional — only if reconciling entitlements via RC REST
# (The iOS public SDK key lives in the Expo app config under apps/mobile, not here.)

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Code execution (Piston)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Self-hosted Piston (https://github.com/engineer-man/piston) powers `code_write`
# quiz questions — the learner's code is run in a sandbox container and graded
# against test cases. Runtime-only secret; set it in Coolify's runtime env.
#
# When unset, /api/quiz/code-execute returns 503 and the editor shows
# "the code runner isn't available right now" — i.e. code does not run at all.
# Point this at the Piston container's base URL (NO trailing /api/v2 — the
# client appends it). Install language packages on the container, e.g.:
#   cli/index.js ppman install python javascript typescript java c++ sqlite3 go rust
# PISTON_URL=http://piston:2000

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenRouter — GLM models (Haiku / Sonnet replacement)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenRouter is an OpenAI-compatible router. We route the GLM models through it
# for a single live-cost dashboard: GLM-4.7 → the former Haiku slots,
# GLM-4.7-flash → the cheap high-volume structured slots (basic path quiz/
# flashcards, exam mock, weakness sessions, chat generate/intent), GLM-5.2 →
# the former Sonnet slots. The independent quiz verifier also routes Gemini
# 2.5 Flash-Lite through OpenRouter. Other Gemini calls stay Google-direct.
# Server-only RUNTIME secret — set it in Coolify's runtime env, NOT
# with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Create a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
# Leaving this unset changes NO current behavior: the OpenRouter client only
# throws if something actually calls it, and nothing routes to GLM until you
# ALSO point a feature's per-model env override at a GLM token (a later wiring
# step). Until then it's used only by scripts/test-glm-openrouter.ts.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
#
# Optional — exact GLM model slugs on OpenRouter. Defaults shown (confirmed in
# the catalog 2026-07-02). Z.ai rotates point releases (4.6 → 4.7 → 5 → 5.2),
# so the flagship slug in particular may move — re-check if a call 404s.
# GLM_HAIKU_MODEL=z-ai/glm-4.7
# GLM_SONNET_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.2
# GLM_FLASH_MODEL=z-ai/glm-4.7-flash
# DEEPSEEK_FLASH_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
# OPENROUTER_QUIZ_VERIFIER_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite
#
# Quiz verification is cost-bounded: every final exam plus a stable sample of
# ordinary path quizzes. The default sample is 10%; set 0 to verify only final
# exams, 1 to verify every quiz, or disable the verifier entirely.
# QUIZ_VERIFIER_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1
# QUIZ_VERIFIER_DISABLED=0
#
# Optional — attribution shown in OpenRouter's app rankings (harmless to omit).
# OPENROUTER_SITE_URL=https://notemage.app
#
# Optional — comma-separated OpenRouter upstream provider slugs to PREFER (in
# order). OpenRouter load-balances z-ai/* across upstreams and only some support
# prompt caching, so cache hits are inconsistent. Set this to `z-ai` to prefer
# the caching-capable upstream first; fallbacks stay enabled so a down upstream
# still routes (caching when available, availability always). Leave unset for
# OpenRouter's default load-balancing.
# OPENROUTER_PROVIDER_ORDER=z-ai
#
# EXPERIMENT-ONLY — OFF by default. Turns GLM reasoning back ON for the single
# Stage A "structure" call of path generation (never Stage B theory/flashcards/
# quiz, and never a featureOverride call like path-preview). Path generation's
# structure calls otherwise send `reasoning: { enabled: false }` (see
# path-generator-openrouter.ts) because thinking tokens can eat the output
# budget; this experiment measures whether reasoning improves structure quality
# enough to be worth that truncation risk on just the one call per path.
# Valid values: low | medium | high. Anything else (including unset) leaves
# reasoning off, so leaving this unset changes NO current behavior.
# PATH_STRUCTURE_REASONING=high
#
# EXPERIMENT-ONLY — OFF by default. Batches a `learning` slot's theory section
# AND its flashcards into ONE GLM call instead of two (1 call instead of 2 per
# learning slot, only when that slot's calls resolve to the openrouter/GLM
# provider — never on the Anthropic/Gemini MODEL_COMPOSITION_LEGACY rollback,
# and never for review/assessment slots, which are untouched). Measures the
# batching cost saving from plans/glm-path-gen-phase8-batching-eval.md
# empirically instead of by estimate. On ANY failure of the batched call
# (thrown error, truncation, a missing/invalid theory or flashcards part, a
# validation failure) the slot automatically falls back to the existing
# unbatched two-call sequence — a slot can never fail BECAUSE batching failed.
# Valid value: exactly "1". Anything else (including unset) leaves the
# unbatched two-call-per-learning-slot behavior unchanged.
# PATH_LEARNING_BATCH=1
